 ## Background
-The Felzenswalb distance transform was introduced by Felzenswalb and Huttenlocher in 2004, though the reference cites it as 2012 [S1, unofficial]. It is used to generate the scalar distance field required for isosurface extraction [S1, unofficial]. The method is an improvement over the Satherley and Jones method (2001), which uses 8 passes, is not parallelizable, and produces approximations with potential errors [S1, unofficial].
